          "internal": false,
          "note_type_name": "comment",
          "free_text": "Source Clone: OST10017A2"
        }
      ],
      "pcr_assay_conditions": "to perform this experiment in the 96 well format, \n  - the annealing temperature of the primers for each plate must be the \n  same, and \n  - the ORF should have the same size in average (+ - 500 pb) in a plate \n  to adjust the elongation time. \n  use a High Fidelity taq DNA polymerase to diminish the mutation rate \n  inherent to the PCR reaction. \n\n  PCR one reaction: \n\n  10X buffer:  5ul   1X final \n  100mM dNTPs 0,4ul (0,1ul each) 0,2mM final each \n  50 mM MgSO4 2ul   2mM final \n  primer1 20uM  1ul   4uM final \n  primer2 20uM  1ul   4uM final \n  cDNA library  200-400ng   (depending on the size of the ORF) \n  PlatinumHF (Gibco) 0,2ul   up to 0,5ul if necessary \n  H2O  up to 50ul \n\n  PCR condition: \n\n  1- 94C  2' \n  2- 94C  45s \n  3- 54C  1' \n  4- 68C  1'/kb \n  5- go to step 2( 35 times) \n  6- 68C  5' \n  7- 4C for ever\n\n  using Platinum taq from Invitrogen",
      "pcr_assay_method_name": "PCR",
      "pcr_template_description": "cDNA library 200-400ng (depending on the size of the ORF)",
